// RUNTIME contract, replayed WITHOUT validation. This policy intentionally
// FAILS static validation: `context.input.document` is absent from `Ping`, which
// the validator now rejects — see the expected-failure case
// `2093_provider_arg_absent_from_scoped_action`. The replay harness does not run
// the validator (it lowers and evaluates), so this case documents the runtime
// behavior when a deployment skips validation: provider execution is
// unconditional and an absent context field resolves to Null.
//
// Bare `action` scope: this rule (and its provider) covers EVERY action.
// On Read events the provider sees the document; on Ping events the
// document argument is absent -> Null -> the script returns its sentinel
// { length: -1 }, and -1 < 6 holds — so Pings are permitted through the
// SAME provider-gated rule, proving the provider executed there.
permit (
    principal,
    action,
    resource
)
when guardrails {
    Strings::Length(context.input.document).length < 6
};
